<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67576" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρόθεν</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ματρόθεν</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτρο-θε</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>I.</u>
			3.17
		</span></i>), Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτηρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from the mother, by the mother's
				side</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταλέξει ἑωυτὸν μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.173
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Par.</u>
				1.316
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μ. Κρῆσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.99
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>from one's mother</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δεδεγμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					750
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				478
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>from one's mother's womb</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυγόντα μ. σκότον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					664
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				607
			</span></i> (lyr.): with the force of a gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ
				ματρόθεν . . λέκτρ᾽ ἐπλήσω</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				527
			</span></i> (lyr.).— Poet. word, used by <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i>, and in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tox.</u>
				51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alex.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				2.444
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.23
			</span></i>.</div>
